itive number that is less than `instance_count`.\");","path":"scene/resources/multimesh.cpp","commit_id":"e1af7b65b28087f9251eda03a3327e1313c9b51d","original_commit_id":"e615b404aa4be3563d2a095a818a709404195287","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is only correct if you read it as `(0 or a positive number) that is less than ...`, while most everyone would probably read this sentence as `(0) or (a positive number that is less than ...)`, which is incorrect. It also makes it sound like `0` is a special case, which it isn't.\r\n\r\nSo I repeat my suggestion of writing `a non-negative number that is less than ...` (here `number` could also be replaced by `integer`, but that information can already be inferred from the type, so I like `number`).","created_at":"2025-02-01T09:47:02Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T09:54:45Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938241283","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938241283"},"html":