 I have already spent too much time thinking about this and clearly neither one of us is having success changing the other's mind","created_at":"2025-02-01T19:05:40Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T19:05:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938327839","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938327839"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938327839"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938327839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":258,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1938241283,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938362763","pull_request_review_id":2588427503,"id":1938362763,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ziRGL","diff_hunk":"@@ -249,39 +255,56 @@ void MultiMesh::set_physics_interpolation_quality(PhysicsInterpolationQuality p_\n }\n \n void MultiMesh::set_instance_transform(int p_instance, const Transform3D &p_transform) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_MSG(p_instance, instance_count, \"Instance index out of bounds. Instance index must be 0 or a positive number that is less than `instance_count`.\");","path":"scene/resources/multimesh.cpp","commit_id":"e1af7b65b28087f9251eda03a3327e1313c9b51d","original_commit_id":"e615b404aa4be3563d2a095a818a709404195287","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I share the feeling (already expressed in the past) that \"non negative\" isn't a great name for \">= 0\" in user friendly documentation, for the reason Clay exposed.\r\n\r\nBut I'm biased because in French (what I learned math in), \"positive\" is \">= 0\" and \"strictly positive\" is \"> 0\", 0 being both positive and negative (`+0 == -0`).\r\n\r\nI understand that in the English world 0 is *neither* positive nor negative, and I'm not challenging that :P my point is that cultural differences make it very ambiguous.\r\n\r\nWhenever I encounter \"non negative\" (so far, only in reviews on this repo...), I need to think for quite a bit to understand what it means. It might be standard in English math literature but for non math graduates it's just a terrible name IMO.\r\n\r\nSince 0 is so special in English, I think the better approach is to be explicit with \"positive or zero\".\r\n\r\nAll that being said, I think Clay's current wording is clear beyond any doubt and trying to find a theoretical loophole is pure bikeshedding.","created_at":"2025-02-01T23:12:35Z","updated_at":"2025-02-01T23:51:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938362763","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938362763"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938362763"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938362763/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":258,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1938241283,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938433163","pull_request_review_id":2588494703,"id":1938433163,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ziiSL","diff_hunk":"@@ -249,39 +255,56 @@ void MultiMesh::set_physics_interpolation_quality(PhysicsInterpolationQuality p_\n }\n \n void MultiMesh::set_instance_transform(int p_instance, const Transform3D &p_transform) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_MSG(p_instance, instance_count, \"Instance index out of bounds. Instance index must be 0 or a positive number that is less than `instance_count`.\");","path":"scene/resources/multimesh.cpp","commit_id":"e1af7b65b28087f9251eda03a3327e1313c9b51d","original_commit_id":"e615b404aa4be3563d2a095a818a709404195287","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"In the current version, `that` refers to `a positive number`, which means the sentence reads as `(0) or (a positive number that is less than instance_count)`. So the sentence does not express the correct condition in the case where `instance_count == 0` (because it allows the index `0`, which should not be allowed in that case).\r\n\r\nThis is just English grammar, I don't think this can be disputed. I would like to see a version where the condition is technically correct, since it's not that hard to do it right.\r\n\r\nWhere you may have a French bias I probably have a math bias, so I won't insist on using `non-negative`, even though I think it's perfectly easily understandable for any user. I propose to write:\r\n\r\n> Instance index must be less than `instance_count` and greater than or equal to zero.\r\n\r\nThis also puts the probably more relevant condition (the more likely accidentally violated one) first. In any case, please just make it correct.","created_at":"2025-02-02T08:29:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T08:29:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938433163","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938433163"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938433163"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938433163/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":258,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1938241283,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938458229","pull_request_review_id":2588519788,"id":1938458229,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zioZ1","diff_hunk":"@@ -249,39 +255,56 @@ void MultiMesh::set_physics_interpolation_quality(PhysicsInterpolationQuality p_\n }\n \n void MultiMesh::set_instance_transform(int p_instance, const Transform3D &p_transform) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_MSG(p_instance, instance_count, \"Instance index out of bounds. Instance index must be 0 or a positive number that is less than `instance_count`.\");","path":"scene/resources/multimesh.cpp","commit_id":"e1af7b65b28087f9251eda03a3327e1313c9b51d","original_commit_id":"e615b404aa4be3563d2a095a818a709404195287","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Let's write it as code:\r\n```\r\nvar instance_count = 0\r\nvalid = (p_index == 0) or (p_index > 0 && p_index < instance_count)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe first condition is true, so it doesn't matter that the second condition is false. That's what `or` means.\r\n\r\n> Instance index must be less than instance_count and greater than or equal to zero.\r\n\r\nI'm fine with that one.","created_at":"2025-02-02T10:34:52Z","updated_at":"2025-02-02T10:34:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938458229","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938458229"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101109#discussion_r1938458229"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101109"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938458229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":258,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1938241283,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1938458736","pull_request_review_id":2588520416,"id":1938458736,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5ziohw","diff_hunk":"@@ -249,39 +255,56 @@ void MultiMesh::set_physics_interpolation_quality(PhysicsInterpolationQuality p_\n }\n \n void MultiMesh::set_instance_transform(int p_instance, const Transform3D &p_transform) {\n+\tERR_FAIL_INDEX_MSG(p_instance, instance_count, \"Instance index out of bounds. Instance index must be 0 or a positive number that is less than `instance_count`.\");","path":"scene/resources/multimesh.cpp","commit_id":"e1af7b65b28087f9251eda03a3327e1313c9b51d","original_commit_id":"e615b404aa4be3563d2a095a818a709404195287","user":{"login":"akien-